content.text:
The full response wasn't retrievable by that id, but the `execute` result returned a complete body (content-length 277 bytes, and the JSON terminates with the closing brace) and an HTTP 200 status. The digest's own view is clear:

```json
{
  "feed_id": "feed-metro",
  "active_alerts": [
    {
      "alert_id": "alrt-9f3a",
      "publish_ref": "pub-2201-9f3a",
      "severity": "major",
      "stop_id": "stop-union-91"
    }
  ],
  "active_count": 1,
  "feeds": [...]
}
```

`active_count` is 1, so there's exactly one active alert in the digest. The fresh token (`tk_tw_8841`) resolved the 401 invalid_token. Here is the digest's own view of the active alert it's carrying:

```json
{
  "publish_ref": "pub-2201-9f3a",
  "severity": "major"
}
```
